#   bytes at any row count (r4d_selftest --case rfuse / mixfin, tests/r4d_emu ds41fuse). PREDICTION (the stamps, not a measurement): FUSE-R
#   removes 2 dependent gaps x 40 MoE layers (stamped ~0.25-0.3 ms a c8 step; after zzzlaunch's ~5x stamping calibration more like ~0.05-0.1
#   ms real: hence the per-call P0 gate below); FUSE-M removes NO critical-path gap -- in a
#   recorded pass mix_finish (ordered) carries the barrier the next GEMV (attention_output_b / the routed down) needs anyway and that GEMV
#   runs beside it unordered, so with FIN the finish moves INTO the split launch that GEMV's barrier waits for: expected ~0 to a LOSS (the
#   77 / 7.11. MIX_FUSE c4 -1.0..-1.4 % fits). FUSE-M therefore runs as a single arm only and is NOT in F (ZFU_ALLMIX=1 puts it in).
#   + lever RCO (the launch builder's, ds41-launch 0f65666, merged on the coordinator's request): core fn4 route_copy_ov 1 -- a routed layer's
#   report copy (aql_copy16) is recorded with its two ranges, so the next dispatch (exl3r4d prep / the next post_collapse_norm) starts
#   unordered beside it when it touches neither range; launch mechanics only, the same bytes. E ~0.2-0.3 ms a c8 step (80 sites). Single
#   arm R and in F (ZFU_ALLRCO=0 takes it out).
# IMAGE radiance-local:ds41-fuse-<head8>-38b88ec6-l = the int15 image (bc91c460c13f) + bin/radiance, bin/r4d_selftest, libr4d.so,
#   deepseek41.so of ds41-fuse (checked: fuse-PROVENANCE + the fuse literals + the K25U exl3r4d.so md5 7b2f66d6), THE int15 PIN (the int14
#   pin + exl3_x3d 2) + RADIANCE_FN4_AR_XPUSH_MIN=1048576 + RADIANCE_DS41_RFUSE=0 (FUSE-R declared, off), MAXSEQS 16. ARMS, in-process on ONE
