# READINGS, in order:
#   0 P0 (ONE card by chip UUID ZFU_P0_UUID GPU-dbba5c851cfef7b3, no server, before the start): r4d_selftest --case rfuse / mixfin -- every
#     form byte for byte vs the stock launches (a FAIL drops the form: VIRHE, NEEDS USER) + FUSEPERF, the UNSTAMPED per-call times (the stock
#     launches back to back on one stream vs the fused launch; warm = back to back mean, cold = after a 256 MiB read, median; M 1 / 8 / 16 / 48).
#     THE GATE (ds-main-port 13.11., from zzzlaunch: stamped gaps overstate real launch time ~5x, a real dependent gap is ~1 us): a form is
#     KEPT only when it beats the pair by >= ZFU_P0MARGIN_US 1.0 us at M 8 warm AND cold and is not slower cold at M 1 / 16; a dropped form gets
#     no arm and leaves F / Y. NO form kept (ZFU_P0STOP 1): the item STOPS after P0 (~2-3 min, no start) and the FUSEPERF lines are the reading.
#     ZFU_P0ONLY=1: a kbench-only run (stops after P0 whatever the gate says).
#   1 IDENTITY FIRST (strict, T 0 greedy; Y has every switch on, RCO included): the warm-up answers vs stock; a1 (greedy set c1 alone) under B and Y, each vs ref12's a1
#     (+ a1-B vs zzk25s's a1-Z = int15); gs16 (all 16 in flight, cap 48) under Y vs a1-Y; STRICT staggered ld under Y vs a1-Y. ANY
#     difference -> VIRHE and the item STOPS before every speed block.
#   2 c8 WORK-BASED (harness --window gens --gens ZFU_C8GN 2; the same fixed prompts in every block), in-process ZFU_GORDER "B F F B".
#   3 the singles ZFU_SINGLES "R2 R1 R M": one c8 gens block each (decode p50 vs the B blocks).
#   4 c16: one gens block for B and for F (ZFU_C16ARMS "B F").
#   5 1u essay (resprobe essay 512, T 0; the ESSAY RESIDENCY WARM-UP rule): B = one discarded + ZFU_U1N 3 back to back, then F likewise.
# SUMMARY (zzzfuse/fusesum.py, lines "ZFUSE ..."): per block and arm -- agg tok/s; decode-step p50 from the step log over ALL decode steps
#   (THE reading: where the removed gaps are) + the full-row bucket with block separation, the ZFU_POST 10 decode steps after each newcomer /
#   the rest; the matched-prompt newcomer sums; the cycle model; per single arm its decode p50 vs B's two blocks (inside / outside B's range);
#   c16 F vs B; 1u F vs B at matched residency; the GET "fuse" counter deltas per block; the int15 references (zzk25s Z: c8 gens 191.60,
#   decode p50 33.73 ms, c16 236.70, 1u 89.91) as INFO.
